# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for third-party code (dependencies are built
# with TSan via triplets/*-tsan.cmake, so their own races become visible).
# Every entry names the upstream function and why it is benign. Never add
# Cartwheel code here: fix it instead.

# civetweb (prometheus-cpp's HTTP exposer) signals its worker threads to stop
# through a plain `int` stop flag written in mg_stop() and polled in
# worker_thread()/master_thread() without atomics. The workers only observe
# the flag eventually; shutdown joins them before freeing the context.
race:civetweb.c
